// The stock client's distance fog. Include after the PerFrame block (it reads
// view, fogParams and localLightMeta from it).
//
// Wow.exe 3.3.5a: DayNight 0x7f16f0 hands the renderer a fog start, end and
// exponent. 0x873210 uploads them for the M2 shaders as vertex constant c30
// = (-k, k * end, exponent, 0) with k = 1 / (end - start) (0xd4300c, the
// scale on the first term, is only ever 1.0, 0x872d09); vsLiquidWater's c4
// has the same form (0x8a38b0), and terrain.bls reads its c12 the same way
// (that upload is not traced). Every arbvp1 shader (terrain.bls,
// diffuse_t1.bls, color_t1.bls, cdiffuse_t1.bls, vsliquidwater.bls...) writes
//     fogcoord = clamp(pow(max(z * c.x + c.y, 0), c.z), 0, 1)
//              = clamp(((end - z) / (end - start))^exponent, 0, 1)
// with z the view-space depth (not the distance), and that is the fog factor
// itself, D3D's oFog: 1 shows the surface, 0 the fog colour. The exponent is
// 1 on Azeroth and Kalimdor (plain linear fog) and 1.5-7 on maps from 530 on,
// where the end is the far clip; the larger exponents belong to zones whose
// band fog was short, and pull the fog in toward the camera again
// (stock_light_math.hpp).
//
// fogParams.x is the start, .y the end; the exponent rides in
// localLightMeta.y as float bits (every float .w was taken). A block that
// never set it (0) reads as linear.

float stockFogVisibility(vec3 worldPos) {
    float z = -(view * vec4(worldPos, 1.0)).z;
    float range = max(fogParams.y - fogParams.x, 1e-3);
    float e = intBitsToFloat(localLightMeta.y);
    e = e > 0.0 ? e : 1.0;
    float x = max((fogParams.y - z) / range, 0.0);
    return clamp(pow(x, e), 0.0, 1.0);
}
